  "result": "Perfect! All 197 tests pass. Payment terms functionality is now complete.\n\n**What I've implemented:**\n\n1. **Added TERMS_INVALID error** to src/errors.js for invalid payment terms\n2. **Updated createInvoice** to accept an optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n3. **Added terms validation** \u2014 only accepts 'NET14', 'NET30', or 'EOM'\n4. **Added dueDate calculation**:\n   - NET14: 14 days from issue date\n   - NET30: 30 days from issue date  \n   - EOM: last day of the month of the issue date\n5. **Invoice now includes**:\n   - `terms`: the payment terms string\n   - `dueDate`: calculated due date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n6. **Added 17 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Default NET30 behavior\n   - Each term type (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n   - Month/year boundary crossings\n   - Leap year handling for February EOM\n   - Error cases (unknown terms, wrong case, empty string)\n   - Invoice structure verification\n\nThe due date calculation properly handles all edge cases including leap years and month boundaries.",
